Subject: [PATCH 08/16] Web Extensions: webNavigation.onCreatedNavigationTarget
 (Sunset W4)

A page that opens a window (window.open, a link with a target) now gives webNavigation.onCreatedNavigationTarget, with
sourceTabId, sourceFrameId, tabId, url and timeStamp, as in Firefox and Chrome. uBlock Origin blocks pop-ups with it; its
background page stopped at its start when the event was missing.

Fired when the app reports the new tab (didOpenTab) and the tab's page has an opener frame whose page is a tab the
extension knows, with the webNavigation permission on the source tab and access to the new tab's URL (when it has one
yet). A new message, DispatchWebNavigationCreatedNavigationTargetEvent, carries the two tabs.

